				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-439079#post-2758017</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-439079/scpokemon#post-2758017</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 01 Mar 2017 14:59:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>dankaar</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1790336</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Well, you kinda answered your own question there:</p> <blockquote> <p>and they already talked about how he shouldn't be able to control the &quot;pokèmon&quot; he already has.</p> </blockquote> <p>So, until he got into the SCP, they had no idea if he'd be able to control 682 to begin with. So, as far as they're aware of, he could've used 682's Pokeball, and then both he and the entire countryside would shortly be pounded into a pancake by a rampaging 682 while 826 was still missing.</p> <p>As for a <a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WatsonianVersusDoylist">Doylist</a> perspective on why they didn't, the tale would quickly become a series of &quot;682 is immune to damage; kills the other Pokemon and its trainer.&quot; And <em>that</em> would be boring to read.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
